{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Leadership"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Mistakes in Management"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le06ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to keep tabs "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to watch someone or something carefully to check what they are doing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It's tempting to keep tabs on every activity your team engages in."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about managers. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ongoing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "continuing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They will still need adequate direction, ongoing feedback and motivation. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to outline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give the main points but not the details"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Having outlined roles and responsibilities, you ensure that your team understands their duties. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the big picture"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the situation considered as a whole"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many managers take this step, but neglect to give their staff a sense of the big picture."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "input"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ideas that you put into a job or activity in order to help it succeed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some managers are great at giving direction and providing feedback, but they forget to ask for their team's input in return. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "indecisiveness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bstate of being \u200bunable to make a \u200bchoice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Indecisiveness can slow us down at this stage."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hesitation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pausing before doing something, \u200bespecially when you are not \u200bcertain about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Any hesitation on our side is not good."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to impede"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to make it difficult for someone or something to make progress"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That impeded our progress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "productivity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the rate at which something is produced in relation to the work, time, and money needed to produce them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Indecisiveness or hesitation can significantly impede productivity in a business environment. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to procrastinate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to delay doing something that you ought to do, usually because you do not want to do it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Having gathered all the information you need, you avoid procrastinating in reaching a decision."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob03aud10"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reason Clauses: Using a Participle Clause and <span class=\"italic\">Because</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are different ways to construct a sentence with a reason clause. You should try to vary the way you construct sentences to make your English appear more dynamic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li>You can use a <span class=\"underline\">conjunction </span>like <span class=\"italic\">because</span>.</ol></li>For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I made mistakes <span class=\"strong\">because </span>I was tired.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">The team succeeded <span class=\"strong\">because </span>she was the manager. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol start=\"2\"><li> You can use a <span class=\"underline\">participle clause</span> to express reason. </ol></li>For example:<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Being tired</span>, I made mistakes.</span> (= \u2026 because I was tired.) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Crowds were waiting at the airport, <span class=\"strong\">hoping to see the CEO arrive </span>.</span> (= ... because they were hoping to see her arrive.)<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Not feeling very well</span>,  James decided to leave for the day.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Having lost my passport</span>,  I have to apply for a new one.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">The restaurant having closed</span>,  there was nowhere to eat.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Being rather busy</span>,  I completely forgot the time.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many managers take this step, but neglect to give their staff a sense of the big picture because they are caught up with the details."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Having outlined roles and responsibilities, you ensure that your team understands their duties."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " When-Clauses to Express Time"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use an adverbial clause of time with a conjunction. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "To talk about a complete action, you use the conjunction <span class=\"italic\">when </span>to connect the time clause to the rest of the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When I arrived</span>, the meeting was over. <br/>We were discussing the issue <span class=\"strong\">when the manager walked in</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When</span> can also mean <span class=\"italic\">\u201cevery time\u201d</span>. <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When you go to see her</span>, she is always busy. <br/>I walk to the office <span class=\"strong\">when it's nice out</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When they are provided with the information and resources they need, they are able to do their jobs without you attempting to manage their every move. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you first take on a managerial role, it's tempting to keep tabs on every activity your team engages in."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm mistakes you feel a bad manager often makes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change partners and compare."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a story about a personal experience with a bad manager (a former teacher, a coach ...)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make your story about 200 words long."}, {"type": "text", "content": "How was the manager ineffective? What mistakes did they make?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share stories with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare the experiences to the \u201ccommon mistakes managers make\u201d in the lesson dialogue and look for similarities."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm ideas about what makes a bad manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my ideas with others."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about a personal experience with a bad a manager and share stories with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare the stories to the \u201ccommon mistakes managers make.\u201d"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss reasons and results of an event or action related to work and jobs."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk or report about things, actions, events, or people in a work environment."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the mistakes a manager can make."}, {"type": "Free Hea