scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le06ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"underline\">Holding on too tightly to authority<br/></span>\nWhen you first take on a managerial role, it's tempting to keep tabs on every activity your team engages in and to try to be involved in all discussions.</br>It's important to inform your team about your expectations, but you need to teach yourself to then step out of the way. You need to trust your team to determine the most effective way to distribute and complete the work. When they are provided with the information and resources they need, they are able to do their jobs without you attempting to manage their every move.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le06ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "31000", "text": "<span class=\"underline\">Failing to define roles<br/></span>\nAs a manager, you will likely be responsible for overseeing the work of a team. Individuals on the team may have many years' experience in their positions, but this does not mean you should adopt a laissez-faire approach to managing them. They will still need adequate direction, ongoing feedback and motivation. Having outlined roles and responsibilities, you ensure that your team understands their duties. Many managers take this step, but neglect to give their staff a sense of the big picture because they are caught up in all the details.<br/><span class=\"underline\">Failing to listen<br/></span>\nSome managers are great at giving direction and providing feedback, but they forget to ask for their team's input in return. Even junior staff under your supervision can be a source of innovative ideas and new perspectives, but you'll never find out unless you listen to them. When you launch a new project or consider a new process, hold a team brainstorming session.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le06ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "87000", "text": "<span class=\"underline\">Poor decision making<br/></span>\nIndecisiveness or hesitation can significantly impede productivity in a business environment. Having gathered all the information you need, you avoid procrastinating in reaching a decision. When you make a decision, research strategies for making responsible choices or use one of the many tools available for evaluating whether or not to take a specific course of action.</br><span class=\"underline\">Forgetting to recognize and praise staff</span>\n<br/>Carefully delivered critical assessment is necessary because it brings out the best in your team. If you never utter a word of praise when your staff does something right, they will start to feel undervalued or unappreciated.  Simple gestures such as publicly offering praise during a group meeting can go a long way in making staff feel appreciated.</br> Being committed to learn from your mistakes, you'll feel more comfortable and confident in the role of manager.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le06ob03re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob03re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}